WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:37.700
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:37.970 --> 01:44.020
[Small Town Remedy]

3
01:44.090 --> 01:46.880
[Episode 22]

4
02:07.000 --> 02:08.800
Why does this smell so foul?

5
02:10.280 --> 02:11.590
Is it ready now or not?

6
02:12.840 --> 02:14.080
Look who you're asking.

7
02:14.080 --> 02:15.540
How would I possibly know?

8
02:16.560 --> 02:17.960
Just boil it a little longer.

9
02:17.960 --> 02:19.420
Won't it get even thicker?

10
02:20.400 --> 02:21.310
It'll look even more awful.

11
02:21.310 --> 02:22.520
I heard from Ai Chen

12
02:23.590 --> 02:25.079
that she put a lot of effort

13
02:26.590 --> 02:28.470
into curing you.

14
02:30.280 --> 02:31.680
Do you know that?

15
02:32.110 --> 02:32.910
I know.

16
02:34.280 --> 02:35.120
Are you moved?

17
02:35.910 --> 02:36.710
A little.

18
02:37.240 --> 02:38.400
Just a little?

19
02:40.310 --> 02:41.110
Just a little.

20
02:41.840 --> 02:43.040
A little also counts.

21
02:45.630 --> 02:47.560
But I heard that

22
02:49.120 --> 02:51.120
you haven't been very cooperative.

23
02:51.590 --> 02:53.190
That's not true.

24
02:54.000 --> 02:56.060
It's just too hard to cure my illness.

25
02:56.680 --> 02:59.079
No matter what, you must accept treatment.

26
03:01.150 --> 03:02.190
Sit closer.

27
03:10.710 --> 03:11.630
A bit closer.

28
03:19.400 --> 03:20.560
I also heard that

29
03:22.520 --> 03:24.680
you've made up your mind.

30
03:24.680 --> 03:26.240
Mm-hmm.

31
03:26.240 --> 03:27.630
I want to treat this illness,

32
03:27.630 --> 03:29.150
but it can't be cured.

33
03:29.150 --> 03:31.120
That's not a contradiction, right?

34
03:31.120 --> 03:32.650
And I also heard from Ai Chen

35
03:32.750 --> 03:34.870
that Mrs. Mi Si also has kleptomania.

36
03:34.870 --> 03:35.430
Why haven't you

37
03:35.430 --> 03:36.750
gotten it treated all these years?

38
03:36.750 --> 03:38.750
Liu Zhengliang! Come take a look!

39
03:39.400 --> 03:40.150
S-She's calling me over.

40
03:40.150 --> 03:41.480
I'm going to take a look.

41
03:43.750 --> 03:46.280
It's going to burn on the bottom if we keep boiling it, right?

42
03:46.280 --> 03:47.079
What's wrong?

43
03:47.590 --> 03:48.840
See if it's done.

44
03:49.360 --> 03:50.470
I can't tell

45
03:50.470 --> 03:51.520
if it's done either.

46
03:51.520 --> 03:52.360
Fine.

47
03:53.000 --> 03:54.800
I'll just leave it at this state.

48
03:55.360 --> 03:57.590
We might as well give it a shot.

49
03:58.120 --> 03:59.520
Here you are. Bottoms up.

50
04:00.310 --> 04:01.360
Wait, what do you mean?

51
04:01.360 --> 04:02.630
There's some for me, too?

52
04:02.630 --> 04:03.680
Yes, of course.

53
04:04.030 --> 04:05.150
One bowl for you, and one for me.

54
04:05.150 --> 04:06.470
It cures any disease.

55
04:06.590 --> 04:07.400
No, no...

56
04:08.150 --> 04:09.030
Didn't you get

57
04:09.030 --> 04:10.080
this folk remedy to cure

58
04:10.080 --> 04:11.870
your nausea whenever you see written words?

59
04:11.870 --> 04:13.000
Mine is for that.

60
04:13.150 --> 04:15.150
Yours is for treating your fear of snow.

61
04:15.150 --> 04:16.160
We both have to drink it.

62
04:16.160 --> 04:17.490
But they're different.

63
04:18.160 --> 04:19.390
I-I can't drink this kind

64
04:19.390 --> 04:21.040
of stuff with unknown ingredients.

65
04:21.040 --> 04:21.839
Just drink it.

66
04:22.240 --> 04:23.240
It won't kill you.

67
04:23.240 --> 04:25.370
That still doesn't mean I can drink it.

68
04:26.000 --> 04:27.830
Besides, it might kill me.

69
04:28.750 --> 04:30.680
I advise you not to drink it either.

70
04:30.830 --> 04:31.760
Liu Zhengliang.

71
04:34.480 --> 04:36.480
I really appreciate how you treat patients

72
04:36.480 --> 04:37.800
ridiculously.

73
04:38.600 --> 04:39.390
However,

74
04:40.040 --> 04:40.830
you need to care more

75
04:40.830 --> 04:42.159
about your own illness.

76
04:42.430 --> 04:43.270
You need to be

77
04:43.270 --> 04:44.750
as brave as I am.

78
04:45.040 --> 04:45.720
Cheers.

79
04:47.000 --> 04:49.240
Did you mean "meticulously"?

80
04:54.720 --> 04:55.600
T-This is not

81
04:55.600 --> 04:56.730
a matter of bravery.

82
05:03.000 --> 05:04.160
I won't force you to drink it.

83
05:04.160 --> 05:04.830
Don't...

84
05:07.270 --> 05:08.070
Look.

85
05:08.360 --> 05:09.820
She set an example for you.

86
05:09.830 --> 05:10.630
Drink it.

87
05:37.190 --> 05:38.000
Sorry.

88
05:38.540 --> 05:40.740
[1314 Funeral Supplies] [Xiaoximen Store]

89
05:51.390 --> 05:52.250
How do you feel?

90
05:54.240 --> 05:55.270
A bit better.

91
05:56.190 --> 05:57.250
What did I tell you?

92
05:57.600 --> 05:59.730
You can't drink random things, right?

93
06:00.830 --> 06:01.600
You did say that.

94
06:01.600 --> 06:02.400
This thing...

95
06:04.480 --> 06:06.080
It's good as long as it works.

96
06:06.430 --> 06:07.560
I used to

97
06:08.160 --> 06:10.270
throw up after reading too much.

98
06:10.630 --> 06:12.480
Now, I already feel nauseous

99
06:12.480 --> 06:13.880
before I even open a book.

100
06:15.000 --> 06:16.270
Still so obstinate.

101
06:17.000 --> 06:17.830
Wipe it.

102
06:20.000 --> 06:20.800
Listen.

103
06:21.680 --> 06:23.540
Do you think I was messing around?

104
06:24.680 --> 06:26.120
Mine was medicine.

105
06:26.120 --> 06:26.830
What I gave you was

106
06:26.830 --> 06:28.270
a winter melon and tangerine peel Americano,

107
06:28.270 --> 06:29.040
okay?

108
06:29.160 --> 06:29.950
Just to give you

109
06:29.950 --> 06:31.630
a little placebo effect.

110
06:35.950 --> 06:36.630
Well,

111
06:36.630 --> 06:37.480
placebo effect

112
06:37.480 --> 06:38.720
only works

113
06:38.720 --> 06:39.720
if I believe it.

114
06:43.000 --> 06:43.800
You.

115
06:45.159 --> 06:46.240
Come out with me.

116
06:46.240 --> 06:47.360
What are you doing?

117
06:48.190 --> 06:49.050
What am I doing?

118
06:49.070 --> 06:49.600
Just for a chat.

119
06:49.600 --> 06:50.659
Alright, alright.

120
06:51.950 --> 06:53.120
D-Don't give him a hard time.

121
06:53.120 --> 06:54.310
Stay out of this.

122
06:55.920 --> 06:57.830
This is a conversation

123
06:58.360 --> 06:59.190
between men.

124
07:00.600 --> 07:01.360
Let's go.

125
07:09.950 --> 07:11.550
Will they fight to the death?

126
07:12.120 --> 07:13.850
Your dad knows what he's doing.

127
07:14.430 --> 07:15.820
I'm feeling so nauseous.

128
07:15.820 --> 07:19.570
[Burial Items]

129
07:21.560 --> 07:23.310
Don't be nervous.

130
07:25.750 --> 07:26.800
I'm not nervous.

131
07:27.240 --> 07:28.070
Well,

132
07:28.480 --> 07:30.680
if you want to beat me up,

133
07:30.750 --> 07:32.070
just do it.

134
07:32.390 --> 07:33.830
I can't beat you anyway,

135
07:33.950 --> 07:35.150
so I won't fight back.

136
07:36.120 --> 07:37.680
Why would I beat you up?

137
07:38.310 --> 07:39.680
I know I'm annoying.

138
07:40.070 --> 07:42.270
No one has ever liked me since I was a kid.

139
07:44.680 --> 07:46.140
I don't know about others,

140
07:46.870 --> 07:50.240
but I'm really fond of you.

141
07:58.159 --> 07:59.360
What you're saying is...

142
07:59.360 --> 08:01.160
is giving me goosebumps.

143
08:03.040 --> 08:04.240
I have my principles.

144
08:04.680 --> 08:05.830
I like whoever

145
08:05.830 --> 08:07.070
my daughter likes.

146
08:08.510 --> 08:09.390
Besides,

147
08:11.800 --> 08:12.830
you're

148
08:13.390 --> 08:14.520
quite an honest guy.

149
08:15.040 --> 08:15.830
This is good.

150
08:21.270 --> 08:23.200
Then... Then why did you ask me out?

151
08:37.510 --> 08:38.510
I've been

152
08:38.510 --> 08:40.549
pondering over this all afternoon.

153
08:42.200 --> 08:43.840
I think you've got a point.

154
08:44.790 --> 08:45.750
What do you mean?

155
08:47.510 --> 08:48.840
Back then, you asked me

156
08:48.840 --> 08:51.790
if I ever thought about

157
08:52.200 --> 08:54.600
treating Mi Si's

158
08:54.600 --> 08:56.840
stealing problem.

159
08:59.840 --> 09:01.200
You have no idea.

160
09:04.030 --> 09:05.870
I don't know what else I can do.

161
09:06.510 --> 09:07.320
Hello.

162
09:28.600 --> 09:30.390
It's impossible to stop her in time.

163
09:30.390 --> 09:32.000
I'm really afraid

164
09:32.000 --> 09:34.400
she'll end up in jail again because of this.

165
09:36.630 --> 09:37.960
If we could

166
09:39.120 --> 09:40.480
root out

167
09:40.480 --> 09:41.870
this problem,

168
09:41.870 --> 09:44.080
that would be great.

169
09:44.270 --> 09:45.000
Yeah,

170
09:45.000 --> 09:47.660
it would definitely be good if it could be cured.

171
09:51.670 --> 09:54.150
Can her problem really be cured?

172
09:54.670 --> 09:55.510
Sure.

173
09:56.960 --> 09:58.550
There are actually many patients

174
09:58.550 --> 09:59.750
with this condition.

175
10:00.080 --> 10:01.120
And I've seen

176
10:01.120 --> 10:03.240
many real-life cases in a book.

177
10:03.840 --> 10:04.840
Honestly,

178
10:05.600 --> 10:06.910
her problem is much easier to cure

179
10:06.910 --> 10:08.750
than mine and Ai Chen's.

180
10:12.670 --> 10:14.840
Could you teach me how to cure it?

181
10:18.270 --> 10:19.080
San.

182
10:24.360 --> 10:25.790
What are you doing?

183
10:26.480 --> 10:28.010
I'm looking for something.

184
10:28.720 --> 10:29.790
There was one time

185
10:31.000 --> 10:32.150
when you were grabbing things

186
10:32.150 --> 10:33.200
in the supermarket

187
10:33.200 --> 10:34.750
and got caught on camera.

188
10:35.840 --> 10:37.500
I paid them money to settle it,

189
10:38.120 --> 10:39.510
got the video back,

190
10:39.510 --> 10:40.600
and made a disc of it.

191
10:40.600 --> 10:42.530
But I can't remember where I put it.

192
10:43.000 --> 10:44.030
Did that happen?

193
10:44.870 --> 10:46.070
Why don't I remember?

194
10:47.390 --> 10:49.200
You just don't want to remember.

195
10:50.000 --> 10:51.480
Why are you looking for it?

196
10:51.670 --> 10:52.320
I...

197
10:52.870 --> 10:53.670
I'm just...

198
10:54.390 --> 10:56.270
I'm just trying to cure your problem.

199
10:56.270 --> 10:57.750
What's your problem?

200
10:58.320 --> 11:00.200
You've been influenced by those two.

201
11:00.200 --> 11:02.030
Well, look,

202
11:02.750 --> 11:03.720
Liu Zhengliang

203
11:03.720 --> 11:04.630
actually has some skills.

204
11:04.630 --> 11:06.870
I hate whoever says I have a problem.

205
11:07.440 --> 11:09.570
Okay, let's not say you have a problem.

206
11:09.870 --> 11:10.670
Let's just say

207
11:11.000 --> 11:12.600
we'll find a way

208
11:12.720 --> 11:14.750
to correct your little bad habit.

209
11:14.750 --> 11:15.810
I won't correct it.

210
11:16.670 --> 11:18.270
I'm already this old.

211
11:19.440 --> 11:21.790
Well, aren't you curious?

212
11:22.240 --> 11:23.910
Don't you want to know what exactly

213
11:23.910 --> 11:25.110
Liu Zhengliang said?

214
11:27.000 --> 11:28.030
Let's hear it.

215
11:33.020 --> 11:36.640
[1314 Funeral Services]

216
11:33.550 --> 11:34.280
Just this...

217
11:36.320 --> 11:37.520
What do you want to do?

218
11:37.870 --> 11:39.600
Well, um,

219
11:39.600 --> 11:41.120
I'll find that disc,

220
11:41.120 --> 11:43.080
and then you watch the video. Um...

221
11:43.360 --> 11:44.440
As soon as you see yourself

222
11:44.440 --> 11:45.550
grabbing something,

223
11:45.550 --> 11:46.880
you just slap yourself.

224
11:47.000 --> 11:48.150
You see it, and you

225
11:48.150 --> 11:49.120
slap yourself.

226
11:50.840 --> 11:53.870
Um, this is called aversion therapy.

227
11:54.750 --> 11:55.550
Basically,

228
11:55.720 --> 11:57.270
once you slap yourself,

229
11:57.270 --> 11:58.790
this stimulation

230
11:58.840 --> 12:00.120
will...

231
12:00.440 --> 12:02.360
will suppress your satisfaction

232
12:02.360 --> 12:04.480
of grabbing things.

233
12:06.150 --> 12:07.440
You want to electrocute me?

234
12:07.440 --> 12:08.110
No, no...

235
12:08.150 --> 12:10.120
No, you can't electrocute anyone with this.

236
12:10.120 --> 12:10.870
It just...

237
12:11.550 --> 12:12.550
hurts a little.

238
12:16.780 --> 12:19.420
[To the second floor]

239
12:18.670 --> 12:19.510
Stop there!

240
12:19.550 --> 12:23.790
[Fucheng Huaide Funeral Center]

241
12:21.670 --> 12:24.670
It doesn't hurt? If it doesn't hurt, why are you running?

242
12:24.670 --> 12:25.730
What's wrong, Mom?

243
12:25.750 --> 12:28.080
Go get your dad's clothes.

244
12:35.720 --> 12:36.720
Amy!

245
12:39.720 --> 12:42.550
"I, Yang Guo, swear that my heart

246
12:43.630 --> 12:46.320
only belongs to you, now and forever, Auntie.

247
12:46.630 --> 12:48.150
If I ever betray you,

248
12:48.440 --> 12:50.120
you don't even need to kill me.

249
12:50.630 --> 12:52.750
I will kill myself immediately."

250
12:53.910 --> 12:55.000
After saying that,

251
12:55.000 --> 12:57.320
he broke out in a cold sweat

252
12:57.600 --> 12:58.790
and just gave himself

253
12:58.790 --> 13:00.390
2 heavy slaps.

254
13:03.150 --> 13:04.550
Do you believe in vows?

255
13:05.550 --> 13:06.320
Nope.

256
13:06.510 --> 13:07.840
If vows meant anything,

257
13:07.910 --> 13:10.270
the old factory director at my mom's workplace

258
13:10.270 --> 13:12.400
would have gotten his karma years ago.

259
13:17.150 --> 13:17.910
Jia Xin.

260
13:21.870 --> 13:23.200
I can't see anything.

261
13:23.750 --> 13:25.200
I can only listen.

262
13:27.150 --> 13:27.960
No matter

263
13:28.790 --> 13:30.320
what happens in the future,

264
13:30.630 --> 13:31.870
don't ever lie to me.

265
13:34.720 --> 13:35.320
Okay.

266
13:42.790 --> 13:43.360
Alright.

267
13:43.440 --> 13:45.630
That's it for today?

268
13:46.670 --> 13:47.960
It's about time

269
13:47.960 --> 13:49.240
for me to go to work.

270
13:51.550 --> 13:52.270
Can you take me

271
13:52.270 --> 13:53.800
to your workplace with you?

272
13:54.000 --> 13:54.790
Nope.

273
13:55.030 --> 13:55.840
No, no.

274
13:56.150 --> 13:58.200
My workplace is ominous.

275
13:58.910 --> 14:00.370
I don't buy superstition.

276
14:00.720 --> 14:01.550
Now that you've

277
14:01.550 --> 14:02.810
gotten to know my work,

278
14:02.870 --> 14:04.270
I also want to visit

279
14:04.270 --> 14:05.240
your workplace.

280
14:05.100 --> 14:11.650
[Moxibustion Care] [A healthy physique starts with good self-care]

281
14:07.440 --> 14:08.700
I have to work all night

282
14:09.080 --> 14:10.480
and can't leave halfway.

283
14:10.510 --> 14:11.970
How will you get back then?

284
14:12.390 --> 14:13.920
I have the day off tomorrow.

285
14:14.240 --> 14:15.870
We can chat all night long.

286
14:15.910 --> 14:20.140
[Moxibustion Care] [A healthy physique starts with good self-care]

287
14:19.480 --> 14:20.200
But...

288
14:20.200 --> 14:21.720
Why so many buts?

289
14:22.240 --> 14:23.320
If you don't want to, just say it.

290
14:23.320 --> 14:25.390
I want to. I really want to.

291
14:28.180 --> 14:29.880
[West Gate]

292
14:33.290 --> 14:40.740
[Security Department]

293
14:35.670 --> 14:36.630
Here we are.

294
14:37.030 --> 14:37.840
We've arrived?

295
14:37.840 --> 14:38.600
Yep.

296
14:40.080 --> 14:40.840
Come on.

297
14:41.150 --> 14:41.960
Come in.

298
14:41.310 --> 14:44.970
[Registration]

299
14:42.630 --> 14:43.440
You're here, buddy.

300
14:43.440 --> 14:43.960
Hello.

301
14:44.000 --> 14:45.240
Everything is normal.

302
14:45.240 --> 14:46.270
Is this your girlfriend?

303
14:45.640 --> 14:46.310
[Registration]

304
14:46.870 --> 14:47.750
You can get off work.

305
14:47.750 --> 14:48.840
I'm clocking out. Bye-bye.

306
14:48.840 --> 14:49.630
Bye-bye.

307
14:50.670 --> 14:51.840
Keep going.

308
14:53.510 --> 14:54.510
Sit down, please.

309
14:59.750 --> 15:00.950
Have some warm water.

310
15:01.720 --> 15:02.510
Thank you.

311
15:03.320 --> 15:04.320
Don't mention it.

312
15:15.790 --> 15:16.850
What are you doing?

313
15:18.630 --> 15:19.690
I'm looking at you.

314
15:21.200 --> 15:22.670
What's so good to look at?

315
15:23.510 --> 15:25.040
You're very good-looking.

316
15:26.870 --> 15:28.670
I was ugly when I was a kid.

317
15:29.320 --> 15:31.120
I don't know what I look like now.

318
15:32.030 --> 15:33.320
You're very pretty.

319
15:33.550 --> 15:34.910
You're prettier than those characters

320
15:34.910 --> 15:36.080
like Huang Rong and Little Dragon Maiden.

321
15:36.080 --> 15:37.740
Like, 10,000 times prettier.

322
15:37.960 --> 15:38.720
No, 20,000 times.

323
15:38.720 --> 15:40.320
You're just joking around.

324
15:40.440 --> 15:42.550
You haven't even seen the ones in the novels.

325
15:42.550 --> 15:43.910
I can just imagine.

326
15:43.910 --> 15:46.240
You think they're pretty enough, right?

327
15:47.150 --> 15:47.960
Come and help.

328
15:50.150 --> 15:50.960
Well...

329
15:51.720 --> 15:54.030
I have to go carry someone.

330
15:55.720 --> 15:56.790
Then go ahead.

331
15:56.840 --> 15:58.000
I'll wait for you here.

332
15:58.000 --> 15:59.150
Are you scared?

333
15:59.320 --> 16:01.750
Nope! I won't be scared even in the face of a ghost.

334
16:01.750 --> 16:02.960
I can't see anyway.

335
16:03.510 --> 16:05.200
Alright, then, sit for a while.

336
16:05.200 --> 16:06.260
I'll be right back.

337
16:06.720 --> 16:07.750
Have some warm water.

338
16:07.750 --> 16:08.440
Uh-huh.

339
16:23.240 --> 16:24.170
Let's go, buddy.

340
16:25.080 --> 16:25.840
Let's go.

341
16:26.670 --> 16:27.000
Let's go.

342
16:27.000 --> 16:27.550
Look at you two.

343
16:27.230 --> 16:29.210
[Authorized Personnel Only]

344
16:27.550 --> 16:28.390
You're being lovey-dovey

345
16:28.390 --> 16:29.720
at the entrance of the crematorium.

346
16:29.720 --> 16:30.920
We just got together.

347
16:35.320 --> 16:36.120
Here we go.

348
16:36.270 --> 16:37.440
Don't blindly try

349
16:37.600 --> 16:39.790
those folk remedies again in the future.

350
16:39.790 --> 16:41.520
You have to believe in science.

351
16:42.030 --> 16:43.150
Don't take

352
16:43.270 --> 16:44.730
those medicines anymore.

353
16:44.840 --> 16:46.570
What if they ruin your stomach?

354
16:46.630 --> 16:47.960
What if you get poisoned?

355
16:47.960 --> 16:48.840
If you take them again,

356
16:48.840 --> 16:50.000
you'll have multiple organ failure...

357
16:50.000 --> 16:51.360
Can you stop nagging?

358
16:51.960 --> 16:53.090
Why are you so naggy?

359
16:54.840 --> 16:55.600
Ai Chen.

360
16:55.910 --> 17:02.170
[Late Night Snack] [Meet for drinks and fun]

361
16:57.910 --> 16:58.910
You're here.

362
16:59.030 --> 17:00.150
Come on, cheers.

363
17:00.150 --> 17:01.000
Cheers.

364
17:02.790 --> 17:03.630
Who is that?

365
17:04.510 --> 17:05.310
My client.

366
17:06.640 --> 17:08.349
I handled the funerals

367
17:08.349 --> 17:10.410
for his second great-uncle and aunt.

368
17:10.640 --> 17:12.720
He once pursued me, but I turned him down.

369
17:12.720 --> 17:13.650
Wipe your mouth.

370
17:15.440 --> 17:17.030
You can't have any more beer.

371
17:17.030 --> 17:18.400
You just threw up this morning.

372
17:18.400 --> 17:19.640
Eat slowly.

373
17:19.640 --> 17:20.310
I just

374
17:20.310 --> 17:22.270
threw up too much

375
17:22.310 --> 17:23.640
and emptied my stomach.

376
17:23.960 --> 17:25.480
I need to replenish, you know?

377
17:25.480 --> 17:26.720
Don't replenish blindly.

378
17:26.720 --> 17:27.829
You need to believe in medicine.

379
17:27.829 --> 17:29.830
Why wouldn't I believe in medicine?

380
17:31.830 --> 17:34.200
From your medical perspective,

381
17:34.310 --> 17:35.400
tell me

382
17:35.750 --> 17:37.280
how you treat your illness.

383
17:40.160 --> 17:41.550
I'm talking about you. Why drag me into this?

384
17:41.550 --> 17:42.880
You know about my illness.

385
17:42.880 --> 17:43.590
It's hard to treat.

386
17:43.590 --> 17:44.880
I can't explain it either.

387
17:44.880 --> 17:45.940
There you go again.

388
17:46.640 --> 17:48.110
I'm tired of hearing this.

389
17:48.160 --> 17:48.640
What did you

390
17:48.640 --> 17:49.880
